14.4030234Z -               'The existence of an encoding error in a module may suggest other problems as well. Either the module is never imported in practice and could be deleted or a `try` statement around the import is mistakenly discarding the `SyntaxError`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4030322Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4030415Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4030546Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4030978Z +               'Change the format to match the arguments and ensure that the right hand side is always a mapping.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4031745Z -               'Fixing the encoding error is the obvious fix. However, it is worth investigating why a module containing an encoding error was able to persist and address that problem as well.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4031832Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4032725Z -               'If a different encoding should be used for the file, specify it explicitly by putting an encoding specification at the top of the file. For instance, to specify UTF-8 encoding, add the line `# coding=utf-8`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4032934Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4033067Z +               '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4034158Z +               'In the following example the right hand side of the formatting operation can be a `tuple`, which is not a mapping. To fix this example, ensure that `args` is a mapping when `unlike_condition` occurs.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4034253Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4034348Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4034474Z +               '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4034563Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4034711Z +               'def unsafe_format():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4034876Z +               '    if unlikely_condition():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4035023Z +               '        args = (1,2,3)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4035147Z +               '    else:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4035318Z +               '        args = {a:1,b:2,c:3}\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4035504Z +               '    return "%(a)s %(b)s %(c)s" % args\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4035612Z +               '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4035704Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4035826Z                 '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4036499Z +               '* Python Library Reference: [String Formatting.](http://docs.python.org/library/stdtypes.html#string-formatting)\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4036701Z +             text: '# Formatted object is not a mapping\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4038518Z +               'If a format string includes conversion specifiers of the form `%(name)s` then the right hand side of the operation must be a mapping. A string is a format string if it appears on the left of a modulo (`%`) operator, the right hand side being the value to be formatted. If the right hand side is not a mapping then a `TypeError` will be raised. Mappings are usually `dict`s but can be any type that implements the mapping protocol.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4039307Z -               '* Python PEPs: [PEP 263 — Defining Python Source Code Encodings.](https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0263/)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4039776Z -               '* Python Tutorial: [SyntaxErrors.](http://docs.python.org/tutorial/errors.html#syntax-errors)\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4039938Z -             text: '# Encoding error\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4040907Z -               'Encoding errors prevent a module being evaluated and thus imported. An attempt to import a module with an invalid encoding will fail; a `SyntaxError` will be raised. Note that in Python 2, the default encoding is ASCII.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4040991Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4042008Z -               'The existence of an encoding error in a module may suggest other problems as well. Either the module is never imported in practice and could be deleted or a `try` statement around the import is mistakenly discarding the `SyntaxError`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4042094Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4042184Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4042310Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4042748Z +               'Change the format to match the arguments and ensure that the right hand side is always a mapping.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4043524Z -               'Fixing the encoding error is the obvious fix. However, it is worth investigating why a module containing an encoding error was able to persist and address that problem as well.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4043612Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4044810Z -               'If a different encoding should be used for the file, specify it explicitly by putting an encoding specification at the top of the file. For instance, to specify UTF-8 encoding, add the line `# coding=utf-8`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4044899Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4045034Z +               '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4046045Z +               'In the following example the right hand side of the formatting operation can be a `tuple`, which is not a mapping. To fix this example, ensure that `args` is a mapping when `unlike_condition` occurs.\n' +
