2026-10-20T21:06:14.4281830Z             help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4282310Z +             markdown: '# Formatting string mixes implicitly and explicitly numbered fields\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4283454Z +               'A formatting expression, that is an expression of the form `the_format.format(args)` or `format(the_format, args)`, can use explicitly numbered fields, like `{1}`, or implicitly numbered fields, such as `{}`, but it cannot use both. Doing so will raise a `ValueError`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4283738Z -             markdown: '# Wrong number of arguments in a class instantiation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4284553Z -               'A call to the `__init__` method of a class must supply an argument for each parameter that does not have a default value defined, so:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4284644Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4285020Z -               '* The minimum number of arguments is the number of parameters without default values.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4285776Z -               '* The maximum number of arguments is the total number of parameters, unless the class `__init__` method takes a varargs (starred) parameter in which case there is no limit.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4285866Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4285986Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4286535Z +               'Use either explicitly numbered fields or implicitly numbered fields, but be consistent.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4287027Z -               'If there are too few arguments then check to see which arguments have been omitted and supply values for those.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4287107Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4287547Z -               'If there are too many arguments then check to see if any have been added by mistake and remove those.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4287633Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4287788Z +               '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4288328Z +               'In the following example the formatting uses both implicit, `{}`, and explicit, `{1}`, numbering for fields, which is illegal.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4288946Z -               'Also check where a comma has been inserted instead of an operator or a dot. For example, the code is `obj,attr` when it should be `obj.attr`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4289031Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4289681Z -               'If it is not clear which are the missing or surplus arguments, then this suggests a logical error. The fix will then depend on the nature of the error.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4289768Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4289859Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4289984Z -               '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4290074Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4290185Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4290337Z +               'def illegal_format():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4290511Z +               '    "{} {1}".format("spam", "eggs")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4290662Z -               'class Point(object):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4290828Z -               '    def __init__(self, x, y):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4290972Z -               '        self.x = x\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4291114Z -               '        self.y = y\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4291193Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4291427Z -               'p = Point(1)      # TypeError: too few arguments\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4291658Z -               'p = Point(1,2,3)  # TypeError: too many arguments\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4291748Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4291837Z                 '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4291922Z                 '\n' +
