2026-10-20T21:06:14.4437091Z +             text: 'Calling super with something other than the enclosing class may cause incorrect object initialization.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4437660Z -             text: 'Descriptor objects can be shared across many instances. Mutating them can cause strange side effects or race conditions.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4437738Z             },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4437825Z             help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4438110Z +             markdown: '# First argument to super() is not enclosing class\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4438629Z +               'The `super` class should be called with the enclosing class as its first argument and `self` as its second argument.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4438938Z -             markdown: '# Mutation of descriptor in `__get__` or `__set__` method\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4439710Z -               'The descriptor protocol allows user programmable attribute access. The descriptor protocol is what enables class methods, static methods, properties and `super()`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4439793Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4441310Z +               'Passing a different class may work correctly, provided the class passed is a super class of the enclosing class and the enclosing class does not define an `__init__` method. However, this may result in incorrect object initialization if the enclosing class is later subclassed using multiple inheritance.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4442362Z -               'Descriptor objects are class attributes which control the behavior of instance attributes. Consequently, a single descriptor is common to all instances of a class and should not be mutated when instance attributes are accessed.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4442444Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4442530Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4442655Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4442958Z +               'Ensure that the first argument to `super()` is the enclosing class.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4443410Z -               'Do not mutate the descriptor object, rather create a new object that contains the necessary state.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4443494Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4443572Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4443689Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4445572Z +               'In this example, the call to `super(Vehicle, self)` in `Car.__init__` is incorrect, as it passes `Vehicle` rather than `Car` as the first argument to `super`. As a result, `super(SportsCar, self).__init__()` in the `SportsCar.__init__` method will not call all `__init__()` methods because the call to `super(Vehicle, self).__init__()` skips `StatusSymbol.__init__()`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4446216Z -               'In this example the descriptor class `MutatingDescriptor` stores a reference to `obj` in an attribute.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4446306Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4446391Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4446498Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4446584Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4446673Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4446835Z +               'class Vehicle(object):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4446961Z +               '    pass\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4447083Z +               '        \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4447233Z +               'class Car(Vehicle):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4447513Z -               '#This is prone to strange side effects and race conditions.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4447705Z -               'class MutatingDescriptor(object):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4447794Z                 '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4447953Z +               '    def __init__(self):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4448193Z +               '        #This is OK provided that Car is not subclassed.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4448388Z +               '        super(Vehicle, self).__init__()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4448531Z +               '        self.car_init()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4448700Z -               '    def __init__(self, func):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4448860Z -               '        self.my_func = func\n' +
