2026-10-20T21:06:14.4462962Z                 '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4463403Z +               '* Python Standard Library: [super](https://docs.python.org/3/library/functions.html#super).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4464069Z +               '* Artima Developer: [Things to Know About Python Super](http://www.artima.com/weblogs/viewpost.jsp?thread=236275).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4464485Z +               '* Common Weakness Enumeration: [CWE-687](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/687.html).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4464749Z +             text: '# First argument to super() is not enclosing class\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4465286Z +               'The `super` class should be called with the enclosing class as its first argument and `self` as its second argument.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4465849Z -               '* Python Language Reference: [Implementing Descriptors.](https://docs.python.org/reference/datamodel.html#descriptors)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4466297Z -               "* Mark Lutz. *Learning Python*, Section 30.6: Methods Are Objects: Bound or Unbound. O'Reilly 2013.\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4466690Z -               '* A real world example: [NumPy Issue 5247.](https://github.com/numpy/numpy/issues/5247)\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4466972Z -             text: '# Mutation of descriptor in `__get__` or `__set__` method\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4467744Z -               'The descriptor protocol allows user programmable attribute access. The descriptor protocol is what enables class methods, static methods, properties and `super()`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4467830Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4469202Z +               'Passing a different class may work correctly, provided the class passed is a super class of the enclosing class and the enclosing class does not define an `__init__` method. However, this may result in incorrect object initialization if the enclosing class is later subclassed using multiple inheritance.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4470248Z -               'Descriptor objects are class attributes which control the behavior of instance attributes. Consequently, a single descriptor is common to all instances of a class and should not be mutated when instance attributes are accessed.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4470334Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4470413Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4470538Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4470845Z +               'Ensure that the first argument to `super()` is the enclosing class.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4471291Z -               'Do not mutate the descriptor object, rather create a new object that contains the necessary state.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4471512Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4471606Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4471717Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4473300Z +               'In this example, the call to `super(Vehicle, self)` in `Car.__init__` is incorrect, as it passes `Vehicle` rather than `Car` as the first argument to `super`. As a result, `super(SportsCar, self).__init__()` in the `SportsCar.__init__` method will not call all `__init__()` methods because the call to `super(Vehicle, self).__init__()` skips `StatusSymbol.__init__()`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4473906Z -               'In this example the descriptor class `MutatingDescriptor` stores a reference to `obj` in an attribute.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4473991Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4474077Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4474187Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4474266Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4474364Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4474522Z +               'class Vehicle(object):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4474647Z +               '    pass\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4474768Z +               '        \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4475050Z +               'class Car(Vehicle):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4475374Z -               '#This is prone to strange side effects and race conditions.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4475568Z -               'class MutatingDescriptor(object):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4475652Z                 '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4475806Z +               '    def __init__(self):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4476052Z +               '        #This is OK provided that Car is not subclassed.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4476239Z +               '        super(Vehicle, self).__init__()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4476389Z +               '        self.car_init()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4476552Z -               '    def __init__(self, func):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4476713Z -               '        self.my_func = func\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4476822Z                 '        \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4476981Z +               'class StatusSymbol(object):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4477171Z -               '    def __get__(self, obj, obj_type):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4477547Z -               '        #Modified state is visible to all instances of C that might call "show".\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4477697Z -               '        self.my_obj = obj\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4477841Z -               '        return self\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4477959Z -               '        \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4478122Z -               '    def __call__(self, *args):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4478339Z -               '        return self.my_func(self.my_obj, *args)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4478427Z                 '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4478573Z +               '    def __init__(self):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4478781Z +               '        super(StatusSymbol, self).__init__()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4478927Z +               '        self.show_off()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4479070Z -               'def show(obj):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4479209Z -               '    print (obj)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4479305Z -               '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4479450Z -               'class C(object):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4479551Z -               '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4479719Z -               '    def __init__(self, value):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4479880Z -               '        self.value = value\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4479980Z                 '        \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4480172Z +               'class SportsCar(Car, StatusSymbol):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4480321Z -               '    def __str__(self):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4480512Z -               '        return ("C: " + str(self.value))\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4480603Z                 '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4480754Z +               '    def __init__(self):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4480978Z +               '        #This will not call StatusSymbol.__init__()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4481305Z +               '        super(SportsCar, self).__init__()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4481482Z +               '        self.sports_car_init()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4481667Z -               '    show = MutatingDescriptor(show)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4481767Z -               '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4481888Z -               'c1 = C(1)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4482015Z -               'c1.show()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4482136Z -               'c2 = C(2)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4482254Z -               'c2.show()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4482394Z -               'c1_show = c1.show\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4482499Z -               'c2.show\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4482617Z -               'c1_show()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4482702Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4482825Z -               '#Outputs:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4482923Z -               '#C: 1\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4483024Z -               '#C: 2\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4483117Z -               '#C: 2\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4483224Z -               '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4483939Z -               'In the following example, the descriptor class `NonMutatingDescriptor` returns a new object every time `__get__` is called.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4484179Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4484281Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4484408Z -               '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4484537Z -               'import types\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4484638Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4484848Z -               '#Immutable version, which is safe to share.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4485051Z -               'class NonMutatingDescriptor(object):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4485157Z -               '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4485324Z -               '    def __init__(self, func):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4485486Z -               '        self.my_func = func\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4485594Z                 '        \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4485780Z +               '#Fix Car by passing Car to super().\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4485983Z +               '#SportsCar does not need to be changed.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4486146Z +               'class Car(Car, Vehicle):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4486334Z -               '    def __get__(self, obj, obj_type):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4486542Z -               '        #Return a new object to each access.\n' +
