2026-10-20T21:06:14.4605599Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4605962Z +               'In this example neither line of the `increment_and_show()` function has any effect.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4606841Z -               'The MRO of class `X` is just `X, object`. The program will fail when the MRO of class `Y` needs to be calculated because `object` precedes `X` in the definition of `Y` but the opposite is true in the MRO of `X`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4606926Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4607445Z +               'The first line, `++x`, has no effect as it applies the unary plus operator twice. Probably the programmer intended `x += 1`\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4607530Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4608134Z +               'The second line, `x.show`, has no observable effect, but it is likely that `x.show()` was intended.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4608230Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4608324Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4608441Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4608577Z -               'class X(object):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4608735Z -               '    def __init__(self):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4608874Z -               '        print("X")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4609010Z -               'class Y(object,X):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4609162Z -               '    def __init__(self):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4609293Z -               '        print("Y")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4609395Z -               '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4609479Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4609634Z +               'def increment_and_show(x):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4609739Z +               '    ++x\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4609864Z +               '    x.show\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4609957Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4610058Z +               '```\n'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4610183Z -               '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4610627Z -               '* Python: [The Python 2.3 Method Resolution Order](http://www.python.org/download/releases/2.3/mro/).\n'
