2026-10-20T21:06:14.4772835Z +             markdown: '# Modification of dictionary returned by locals()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4773737Z +               "The dictionary returned by `locals()` is not a view of the function's locals, but a copy. Therefore, modification of the dictionary returned from `locals()` will not modify the local variables of the function.\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4774082Z -             markdown: '# Inconsistent equality and hashing\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4775160Z -               'A hashable class has an `__eq__` method, and a `__hash__` method that agrees with equality. When a hash method is defined, an equality method should also be defined; otherwise object identity is used for equality comparisons which may not be intended.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4775277Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4776033Z -               'Note that defining an `__eq__` method without defining a `__hash__` method automatically makes the class unhashable in Python 3. (even if a superclass defines a hash method).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4776120Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4776212Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4776339Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
