2026-10-20T21:06:14.4978690Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4981126Z -               'Unfortunately, this means that if more than one base class defines the same attribute, the leftmost base class will effectively override the attribute of the rightmost base class, even though the leftmost base class is not a subclass of the rightmost base class. Unless the methods in question are designed for inheritance, using `super`, then this implicit overriding may not be the desired behavior. Even if it is the desired behavior it makes the code hard to understand and maintain.\n' +
