2026-10-20T21:06:14.5116301Z +             text: "Using a 'delete' statement to delete a local variable is unnecessary, because the variable is deleted automatically when the function exits."
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5117440Z -             text: 'The formatted object must be a mapping when the format includes a named specifier; otherwise a TypeError will be raised."'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5118012Z             },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5118201Z             help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5118566Z +             markdown: '# Unnecessary delete statement in function\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5119885Z +               'Passing a local variable to a `del` statement results in that variable being removed from the local namespace. When exiting a function all local variables are deleted, so it is unnecessary to explicitly delete variables in such cases.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5120986Z -             markdown: '# Formatted object is not a mapping\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5123090Z -               'If a format string includes conversion specifiers of the form `%(name)s` then the right hand side of the operation must be a mapping. A string is a format string if it appears on the left of a modulo (`%`) operator, the right hand side being the value to be formatted. If the right hand side is not a mapping then a `TypeError` will be raised. Mappings are usually `dict`s but can be any type that implements the mapping protocol.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5124768Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5124975Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5125219Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5125555Z +               'Remove the `del` statement.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5126194Z -               'Change the format to match the arguments and ensure that the right hand side is always a mapping.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5126700Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5126899Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5127133Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5128384Z +               'In the function below, the variable `x` is assigned a value that is used for a calculation, and is then explicitly deleted before the function exits. In this case, the delete statement can be removed without changing the behavior of the function.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5130251Z -               'In the following example the right hand side of the formatting operation can be a `tuple`, which is not a mapping. To fix this example, ensure that `args` is a mapping when `unlike_condition` occurs.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5131077Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5131280Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5131517Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5131831Z +               'def unnecessary_delete():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5132180Z +               '    x = get_some_object()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5132636Z +               '    do_calculation(x)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5133081Z +               '    del x                       # This del statement is unnecessary\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5133432Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5133693Z -               'def unsafe_format():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5133977Z -               '    if unlikely_condition():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5134134Z -               '        args = (1,2,3)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5134262Z -               '    else:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5134418Z -               '        args = {a:1,b:2,c:3}\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5134603Z -               '    return "%(a)s %(b)s %(c)s" % args\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5134686Z                 '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5134772Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5134891Z                 '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5135377Z +               "* Python: [The 'del' statement](https://docs.python.org/2/reference/simple_stmts.html#the-del-statement).\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5135833Z +               '* Python/C API Reference Manual: [Reference counts](https://docs.python.org/2.0/api/refcounts.html).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5136063Z +             text: '# Unnecessary delete statement in function\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5137164Z +               'Passing a local variable to a `del` statement results in that variable being removed from the local namespace. When exiting a function all local variables are deleted, so it is unnecessary to explicitly delete variables in such cases.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5137684Z -               '* Python Library Reference: [String Formatting.](http://docs.python.org/library/stdtypes.html#string-formatting)\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5137887Z -             text: '# Formatted object is not a mapping\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5139686Z -               'If a format string includes conversion specifiers of the form `%(name)s` then the right hand side of the operation must be a mapping. A string is a format string if it appears on the left of a modulo (`%`) operator, the right hand side being the value to be formatted. If the right hand side is not a mapping then a `TypeError` will be raised. Mappings are usually `dict`s but can be any type that implements the mapping protocol.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5139770Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5139856Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5139982Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5140139Z +               'Remove the `del` statement.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5140573Z -               'Change the format to match the arguments and ensure that the right hand side is always a mapping.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5140654Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5140741Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5140858Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5141907Z +               'In the function below, the variable `x` is assigned a value that is used for a calculation, and is then explicitly deleted before the function exits. In this case, the delete statement can be removed without changing the behavior of the function.\n' +
