2026-10-20T21:06:14.5153475Z             },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5153564Z             help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5154161Z +             markdown: '# An assert statement has a side-effect\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5155446Z +               'All code defined in assert statements is ignored when optimization is requested, that is, the program is run with the `-O` flag. If an assert statement has any side-effects then the behavior of the program changes when optimization is requested.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5155666Z -             markdown: '# Unhashable object hashed\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5157243Z -               'If an object is used as a key in a dictionary or as a member of a set then it must be hashable, that is it must define a `__hash__` method. All built-in immutable types are hashable, but mutable ones are not. Common hashable types include all numbers, strings (both `unicode` and `bytes`) and `tuple`. Common unhashable types include `list`, `dict` and `set`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5157341Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5158560Z -               "In order to store a key in a `dict` or `set` a hash value is needed. To determine this value the built-in function `hash()` is called which in turn calls the `__hash__` method on the object. If the object's class does not have the `__hash__` method, then a `TypeError` will be raised.\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5158651Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5158748Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5158940Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5159251Z +               'Move all expressions with side-effects out of assert statements.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5160578Z -               'Since this problem usually indicates a logical error, it is not possible to give a general recipe for fixing it. Mutable collections can be converted into immutable equivalents where appropriate. For example sets can be hashed by converting any instances of `set` into `frozenset` instances.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5160659Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5160748Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5160860Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5162538Z +               'In the example, the exit code from `subprocess.call()` is checked against 0, but the entire expression is called from within an `assert` statement. If the code is ever run, then the not only the assertion itself, but also the external call, will be discarded. It is better to save the result of `subprocess.call()` to a temporary variable, and to assert that variable to be 0.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5163171Z -               '`list`s are not hashable. In this example, an attempt is made to use a `list` as a key in a mapping which will fail with a `TypeError`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5163261Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5163343Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5163458Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5163679Z +               "assert subprocess.call(['run-backup']) == 0\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5163766Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5164142Z -               'def lookup_with_default_key(mapping, key=None):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5164292Z -               '    if key is None:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5164488Z -               '        key = [] # Should be key = ()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5164661Z -               '    return mapping[key]\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5164757Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5164849Z                 '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5164942Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5165058Z                 '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5165722Z +               '* Python Language Reference: [The assert statement](http://docs.python.org/2/reference/simple_stmts.html#assert).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5166352Z +               '* TutorialsPoint, Python Programming: [Assertions in Python](http://www.tutorialspoint.com/python/assertions_in_python.htm).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5166574Z +             text: '# An assert statement has a side-effect\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5167853Z +               'All code defined in assert statements is ignored when optimization is requested, that is, the program is run with the `-O` flag. If an assert statement has any side-effects then the behavior of the program changes when optimization is requested.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5168287Z -               '* Python Standard Library: [hash](http://docs.python.org/library/functions.html#hash).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5168833Z -               '* Python Language Reference: [object.__hash__](http://docs.python.org/reference/datamodel.html#object.__hash__).\n' +
