2026-10-20T21:06:14.5189482Z             help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5189648Z +             markdown: '# Unnecessary pass\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5191438Z +               'A `pass` statement is only necessary when it is the only statement in a block (the list of statements forming part of a compound statement). This is because the purpose of the ` pass` statement is to allow empty blocks where they would otherwise be syntactically invalid. If the block already contains other statements then the `pass` statement is unnecessary.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5191630Z -             markdown: "# 'apply' function used\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5192382Z -               "The 'apply' function is deprecated and makes code harder to read as most Python programmers will not be familiar with it (it has been deprecated since 2003).\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5192590Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5192691Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5192816Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5193001Z +               'Remove the `pass` statement.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5193280Z -               'Replace `apply(function, args)` with `function(*args)`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5193366Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5193738Z -               'Replace `apply(function, args, keywords)` with `function(*args, **keywords)`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5193935Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5194039Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5194159Z                 '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5194572Z +               '* Python: [pass](http://docs.python.org/2/tutorial/controlflow.html#pass-statements).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5194737Z +             text: '# Unnecessary pass\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5196443Z +               'A `pass` statement is only necessary when it is the only statement in a block (the list of statements forming part of a compound statement). This is because the purpose of the ` pass` statement is to allow empty blocks where they would otherwise be syntactically invalid. If the block already contains other statements then the `pass` statement is unnecessary.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5197017Z -               '* Python Standard Library: [apply](http://docs.python.org/2/library/functions.html#apply).\n' +
