2026-10-20T21:06:14.5207127Z             help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5207344Z +             markdown: "# Should use a 'with' statement\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5208157Z +               'The `with` statement was introduced by PEP343 to allow standard uses of `try-finally` statements to be factored out. Using this simplification makes code easier to read.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5208349Z -             markdown: '# Testing equality to None\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5209754Z -               'When you compare an object to `None`, use `is` rather than `==`. `None` is a singleton object, comparing using `==` invokes the `__eq__` method on the object in question, which may be slower than identity comparison. Comparing to `None` using the `is` operator is also easier for other programmers to read.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5209845Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5209932Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5210060Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5211172Z +               'Review the code and determine whether or not the `try-finally` is used only to ensure that a resource is closed. If the only purpose is to ensure that a resource is closed, then replace the `try-finally` statement with a `with` statement.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5211332Z -               'Replace `==` with `is`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5211422Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5211508Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5211620Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5212650Z +               'The following code shows examples of different ways of ensuring that a file is always closed, even when an error is generated. In the second example, the `try-finally` block is replaced by a simpler `with` statement.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5213230Z -               'The `filter2` function is likely to be more efficient than the `filter1` function because it uses an identity comparison.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5213315Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5213403Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5213596Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5213682Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5213956Z +               'f = open("filename")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5214219Z +               'try:                         # Method of ensuring file closure\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5214364Z +               '    f.write(...)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5214495Z +               'finally:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5214630Z +               '    f.close()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5214834Z -               'def filter1(function, iterable=None)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5215094Z -               "    if iterable == None:    # Comparison using '__eq__'\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5215477Z -               '        return [item for item in iterable if item]\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5215617Z -               '    else:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5215899Z -               '        return [item for item in iterable if function(item)]\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5215984Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5216185Z -               'def filter2(function, iterable=None)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5216440Z -               '    if iterable is None:    # Comparison using identity\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5216674Z -               '        return [item for item in iterable if item]\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5216805Z -               '    else:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5217074Z -               '        return [item for item in iterable if function(item)]\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5217164Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5217499Z +               'with open("filename") as f:  # Simpler method of ensuring file closure\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5217640Z +               '    f.write(...)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5217735Z                 '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5217824Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5217938Z                 '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5218622Z +               '* Python Language Reference: [The with statement](http://docs.python.org/reference/compound_stmts.html#the-with-statement).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5219193Z +               '* Python Standard Library: [Context manager ](http://docs.python.org/library/stdtypes.html#context-manager-types).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5219577Z +               '* Python PEP 343: [The "with" Statement](http://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0343).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5219777Z +             text: "# Should use a 'with' statement\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5220588Z +               'The `with` statement was introduced by PEP343 to allow standard uses of `try-finally` statements to be factored out. Using this simplification makes code easier to read.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5221447Z -               '* Python Language Reference: [Comparisons](http://docs.python.org/reference/expressions.html#is), [object.__eq__](http://docs.python.org/reference/datamodel.html#object.__eq__).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5221634Z -             text: '# Testing equality to None\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5223035Z -               'When you compare an object to `None`, use `is` rather than `==`. `None` is a singleton object, comparing using `==` invokes the `__eq__` method on the object in question, which may be slower than identity comparison. Comparing to `None` using the `is` operator is also easier for other programmers to read.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5223123Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5223212Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5223342Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5224579Z +               'Review the code and determine whether or not the `try-finally` is used only to ensure that a resource is closed. If the only purpose is to ensure that a resource is closed, then replace the `try-finally` statement with a `with` statement.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5224748Z -               'Replace `==` with `is`.\n' +
