2026-10-20T21:06:14.5224925Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5225045Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5226075Z +               'The following code shows examples of different ways of ensuring that a file is always closed, even when an error is generated. In the second example, the `try-finally` block is replaced by a simpler `with` statement.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5226733Z -               'The `filter2` function is likely to be more efficient than the `filter1` function because it uses an identity comparison.\n' +
