2026-10-20T21:06:14.5253590Z -               '* Common Weakness Enumeration: [CWE-665](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/665.html).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5253948Z -             text: '# Implicit string concatenation in a list\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5254887Z -               'When two string literals abut each other the Python interpreter implicitly concatenates them into a single string. On occasion this can be useful, but is more commonly misleading or incorrect.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5254973Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5255061Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5255187Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5256302Z +               'Deleting the unreachable code will make the code clearer and preserve the meaning of the code. However, it is possible that the original intention was that the code should execute and that it is unreachable signifies some other error.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5256916Z -               'If the concatenation is deliberate, then use `+` to join the strings. This has no runtime overhead, and makes the intention clear.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5257004Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5257088Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5257206Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5257788Z +               'In this example the assignment to `remainder` is never reached because there is a ` return` statement on the previous line.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5258907Z -               'In the first function below, `unclear`, implicit string concatenation is used twice; once deliberately and once by accident. In the second function, `clarified`, the first concatenation is made explicit and the second is removed.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5258997Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5259160Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5259277Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5259416Z +               'import math\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5259499Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5259650Z +               'def my_div(x, y):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5259825Z +               '    return math.floor(x / y)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5260028Z +               '    remainder = x - math.floor(x / y) * y\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5260175Z -               'def unclear():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5260578Z -               '    # Returns [ "first part of long string and the second part", "/usr/local/usr/bin" ]\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5260828Z -               '    return [\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5260924Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5261112Z -               '        "first part of long string"\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5261296Z -               '        " and the second part",\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5261450Z -               '        "/usr/local"\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5261595Z -               '        "/usr/bin"\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5261706Z -               '    ]\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5261808Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5261949Z -               'def clarified():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5262364Z -               '    # Returns [ "first part of long string and the second part", "/usr/local", "/usr/bin" ]\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5262500Z -               '    return [\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5262689Z -               '        "first part of long string" +\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5262872Z -               '        " and the second part",\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5263017Z -               '        "/usr/local",\n' +
