2026-10-20T21:06:14.5312057Z -             markdown: '# Wrong number of arguments in a call\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5312544Z -               'A function call must supply an argument for each parameter that does not have a default value defined, so:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5312629Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5313031Z -               '* The minimum number of arguments is the number of parameters without default values.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5313745Z -               '* The maximum number of arguments is the total number of parameters, unless the function takes a varargs (starred) parameter in which case there is no limit.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5313943Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5314074Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5314934Z +               'If the conditional statement is required for debugging or similar then use a variable instead. Otherwise, remove the conditional statement and any associated dead code.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5315436Z -               'If there are too few arguments then check to see which arguments have been omitted and supply values for those.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5315521Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5315974Z -               'If there are too many arguments then check to see if any have been added by mistake and remove those.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5316054Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5316184Z +               '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5316955Z +               'In the first example the `if` statement will always be executed and therefore can be removed. The contents of the statement should be kept though.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5317594Z -               'Also check where a comma has been inserted instead of an operator or a dot. For example, the code is `obj,attr` when it should be `obj.attr`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5317680Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5318806Z +               "In the second example the statement `l = 100` is never executed because `1 > 100` is always false. However, it is likely that the intention was `l > 100` (the number '1' being misread as the letter 'l') and that the test should be corrected, rather than deleted.\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5319482Z -               'If it is not clear which are the missing or surplus arguments, then this suggests a logical error. The fix will then depend on the nature of the error.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5319567Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5319653Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5319775Z +               '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5319896Z +               'if True:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5320122Z +               '    print "True is true!"\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5320218Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5320355Z +               'def limit(l):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5320500Z +               '    if l < -100:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5320637Z +               '        l = -100\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5320773Z +               '    if 1 > 100:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5320898Z +               '        l = 100\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5321027Z +               '    return l\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5321118Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5321218Z +               '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5321314Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5321423Z                 '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5321900Z +               '* Python: [The If Statement](http://docs.python.org/reference/compound_stmts.html#the-if-statement).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5322398Z +               '* Python: [The While Statement](http://docs.python.org/reference/compound_stmts.html#the-while-statement).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5322854Z +               '* Python: [Literals (constant values)](http://docs.python.org/reference/expressions.html#literals).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5323282Z +               '* Common Weakness Enumeration: [CWE-561](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/561.html).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5323697Z +               '* Common Weakness Enumeration: [CWE-570](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/570.html).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5324221Z +               '* Common Weakness Enumeration: [CWE-571](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/571.html).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5324480Z +             text: '# Constant in conditional expression or statement\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5325196Z +               'Using a constant value as a test in a conditional statement renders the statement pointless as only one branch will be run regardless of any other factors.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5325602Z -               '* Python Glossary: [Arguments](https://docs.python.org/2/glossary.html#term-argument).\n' +
