2026-10-20T21:06:14.5352026Z             fullDescription: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5352596Z +             text: 'Using a Break or Return statement in a finally block causes the Try-finally block to exit, discarding the exception.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5353228Z -             text: "A membership test, such as 'item in sequence', with a non-container on the right hand side will raise a 'TypeError'."
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5353317Z             },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5353407Z             help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5353669Z +             markdown: "# 'break' or 'return' statement in finally\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5355069Z +               'When a `break` or `return` statement is used in a `finally` block this causes the `try-finally` block to exit immediately discarding the exception. This is unlikely to be the intention of the developer and makes the code more difficult to read.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5355311Z -             markdown: '# Membership test with a non-container\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5356034Z -               'A membership test, that is a binary expression with `in` or `not in` as the operator, expects that the expression to the right of the operator will be a container.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5356133Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5356907Z -               'As well as standard containers such as `list`, `tuple`, `dict` or `set`, a container can be an instance of any class that has the `__contains__`, `__iter__` or `__getitem__` method.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5356987Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5357082Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5357206Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5357853Z +               'Either move the `break` or `return` statement to immediately after the `finally` block or use an explicit `except` block to handle the exception.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5358849Z -               'Ensure that the right hand side of the expression is a container, or add a guard clause for other cases. For example, if the right side may be a container or `None` then change `if x in seq:` to `if seq is not None and x in seq:`\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5359004Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5359519Z +               'These modifications are behavior changing so you must take care to ensure that the resulting behavior is correct.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5359607Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5359737Z -               '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5360896Z -               'In this example the `NotAContainer` class has no `__contains__`, `__iter__` or `__getitem__` method. Consequently, when the line `if 2 in cont:` is executed a TypeError will be raised. Adding a `__getitem__` method to the `NotAContainer` class would solve the problem.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5360980Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5361075Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5361198Z -               '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5361375Z -               'class NotAContainer(object):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5361470Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5361642Z -               '    def __init__(self, *items):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5361799Z -               '        self.items = items\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5361890Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5362024Z -               'def main():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5362204Z -               '    cont = NotAContainer(1, 2, 3)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5362340Z -               '    if 2 in cont:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5362513Z -               '        print("2 in container")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5362608Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5362704Z -               '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5362801Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5362918Z                 '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5364421Z +               '* Python Language Reference: [ The try statement](http://docs.python.org/2.7/reference/compound_stmts.html#the-try-statement), [ The break statement](http://docs.python.org/2/reference/simple_stmts.html#break), [ The return statement](http://docs.python.org/2/reference/simple_stmts.html#return).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5364847Z +               '* Common Weakness Enumeration: [CWE-584](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/584.html).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5365157Z +             text: "# 'break' or 'return' statement in finally\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5366237Z +               'When a `break` or `return` statement is used in a `finally` block this causes the `try-finally` block to exit immediately discarding the exception. This is unlikely to be the intention of the developer and makes the code more difficult to read.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5366768Z -               '* Python: [Membership test details](http://docs.python.org/reference/expressions.html#membership-test-details).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5367366Z -               '* Python: [The __contains__ method](http://docs.python.org/reference/datamodel.html#object.__contains__).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5367584Z -             text: '# Membership test with a non-container\n' +
