2026-10-20T21:06:14.5448670Z             fullDescription: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5449520Z +             text: 'When a class subclasses multiple base classes and more than one base class defines the same attribute, attribute overriding may result in unexpected behavior by instances of this class.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5450037Z -             text: 'Including surplus arguments in a formatting call makes code more difficult to read and may indicate an error.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5450119Z             },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5450199Z             help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5450442Z +             markdown: '# Conflicting attributes in base classes\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5452195Z +               'When a class subclasses multiple base classes, attribute lookup is performed from left to right amongst the base classes. This form of attribute lookup is called "method resolution order" and is a solution to the [diamond inheritance problem](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multiple_inheritance#The_diamond_problem) where several base classes override a method in a shared superclass.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5452423Z -             markdown: '# Unused argument in a formatting call\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5453724Z -               'A formatting expression, that is an expression of the form `the_format.format(args)` or `format(the_format, args)`, can have any number of arguments, provided that there are enough to match the format. However, surplus arguments are redundant and clutter the code, making it harder to read.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5453930Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5456114Z +               'Unfortunately, this means that if more than one base class defines the same attribute, the leftmost base class will effectively override the attribute of the rightmost base class, even though the leftmost base class is not a subclass of the rightmost base class. Unless the methods in question are designed for inheritance, using `super`, then this implicit overriding may not be the desired behavior. Even if it is the desired behavior it makes the code hard to understand and maintain.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5456589Z -               'It is also possible that surplus arguments indicate a mistake in the format string.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5456677Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5456761Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5456882Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5457314Z +               'There are a number of ways that might be used to address this issue:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5457676Z -               'Check that the format string is correct and then remove any surplus arguments.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5457764Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5458112Z +               '* Override the attribute in the subclass to implement the correct behavior.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5458546Z +               '* Modify the class hierarchy and move equivalent or redundant methods to a common super class.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5458929Z +               '* Modify the method hierarchy, breaking up complex methods into constituent parts.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5459137Z +               '* Use delegation rather than inheritance.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5459216Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5459331Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5461039Z +               'In this example the class `ThreadingTCPServer` inherits from `ThreadingMixIn` and from `TCPServer`. However, both these classes implement `process_request` which means that `ThreadingTCPServer` will inherit `process_request` from `ThreadingMixIn`. Consequently, the implementation of `process_request` in `TCPServer` will be ignored, which may not be the correct behavior.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5461872Z -               'In the following example there are three arguments for the call to the `str.format()` method, but the format string only requires two. The third argument should be deleted.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5461959Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5462042Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5462148Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5462313Z -               'def surplus_argument():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5462529Z -               '    the_format = "{} {}" # Used to be "{} {} {}"\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5462717Z -               '    return the_format.format(1, 2, 3)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5462803Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5462969Z +               'class TCPServer(object):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5463066Z +               '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5463332Z +               '    def process_request(self, request, client_address):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5463547Z +               '        self.do_work(request, client_address)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5463737Z +               '        self.shutdown_request(request)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5463949Z -               '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5464032Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5464140Z +               '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5464294Z +               'class ThreadingMixIn:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5464561Z +               '    """Mix-in class to handle each request in a new thread."""\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5464697Z -               '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5465235Z -               '* Python Library Reference: [String Formatting.](https://docs.python.org/2/library/string.html#string-formatting)\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5465448Z -             text: '# Unused argument in a formatting call\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5466745Z -               'A formatting expression, that is an expression of the form `the_format.format(args)` or `format(the_format, args)`, can have any number of arguments, provided that there are enough to match the format. However, surplus arguments are redundant and clutter the code, making it harder to read.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5466957Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5467213Z +               '    def process_request(self, request, client_address):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5467456Z +               '        """Start a new thread to process the request."""\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5467831Z +               '        t = threading.Thread(target = self.do_work, args = (request, client_address))\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5468014Z +               '        t.daemon = self.daemon_threads\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5468152Z +               '        t.start()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5468655Z -               'It is also possible that surplus arguments indicate a mistake in the format string.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5468740Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5469027Z +               'class ThreadingTCPServer(ThreadingMixIn, TCPServer): pass\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5469109Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5469209Z +               '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5470332Z +               'This can be fixed either by overriding the method, as shown in class `ThreadingTCPServerOverriding` or by ensuring that the functionality provided by the two base classes does not overlap, as shown in class `ThreadingTCPServerChangedHierarchy`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5470469Z -               '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5470829Z -               'Check that the format string is correct and then remove any surplus arguments.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5470914Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5470993Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5471119Z +               '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5471221Z +               '   \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5471649Z +               '#Fixed by overriding. This does not change behavior, but makes it explicit and comprehensible.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5472028Z +               'class ThreadingTCPServerOverriding(ThreadingMixIn, TCPServer):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5472130Z +               '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5472381Z +               '    def process_request(self, request, client_address):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5472879Z +               '        #process_request forwards to do_work, so it is OK to call ThreadingMixIn.process_request directly\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5473206Z +               '        ThreadingMixIn.process_request(self, request, client_address)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5473323Z +               '        \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5473453Z -               '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5474342Z -               'In the following example there are three arguments for the call to the `str.format()` method, but the format string only requires two. The third argument should be deleted.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5474431Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5474753Z +               '#Fixed by separating threading functionality from request handling.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5474908Z +               'class ThreadingMixIn:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5475120Z +               '    """Mix-in class to help with threads."""\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5475207Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5475405Z +               '    def do_job_in_thread(self, job, args):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5475615Z +               '        """Start a new thread to do the job"""\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5475858Z +               '        t = threading.Thread(target = job, args = args)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5475991Z +               '        t.start()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5476121Z -               '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5476280Z -               'def surplus_argument():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5476496Z -               '    the_format = "{} {}" # Used to be "{} {} {}"\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5476690Z -               '    return the_format.format(1, 2, 3)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5476770Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5477118Z +               'class ThreadingTCPServerChangedHierarchy(ThreadingMixIn, TCPServer):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5477219Z +               '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5477553Z +               '    def process_request(self, request, client_address):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5477793Z +               '        """Start a new thread to process the request."""\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5478103Z +               '        self.do_job_in_thread(self.do_work,  (request, client_address))\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5478198Z +               '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5478293Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5478379Z                 '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5478458Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5478577Z                 '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5479155Z +               '* Python Language Reference: [Data model](https://docs.python.org/2/reference/datamodel.html).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5479671Z +               '* Python releases: [The Python 2.3 Method Resolution Order](https://www.python.org/download/releases/2.3/mro/).\n' +
