2026-10-20T21:06:14.5480755Z +             text: '# Conflicting attributes in base classes\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5482506Z +               'When a class subclasses multiple base classes, attribute lookup is performed from left to right amongst the base classes. This form of attribute lookup is called "method resolution order" and is a solution to the [diamond inheritance problem](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multiple_inheritance#The_diamond_problem) where several base classes override a method in a shared superclass.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5483036Z -               '* Python Library Reference: [String Formatting.](https://docs.python.org/2/library/string.html#string-formatting)\n'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5483180Z -           },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5483358Z -           id: 'py/str-format/surplus-argument',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5483539Z -           name: 'py/str-format/surplus-argument',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5483640Z -           properties: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5483916Z -             'problem.severity': 'warning',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5484060Z -             'sub-severity': 'high',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5484617Z -             description: 'Including surplus arguments in a formatting call makes code more difficult to read and may indicate an error.',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5484791Z -             id: 'py/str-format/surplus-argument',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5484914Z -             kind: 'problem',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5485113Z -             name: 'Unused argument in a formatting call',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5485251Z -             precision: 'high',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5485341Z -             tags: [
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5485444Z -               'quality',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5485578Z -               'maintainability',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5485700Z -               'useless-code'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5485783Z -             ]
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5485860Z -           },
