2026-10-20T21:06:14.5486977Z -           fullDescription: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5487569Z -             text: `Using implicit and explicit numbering in string formatting operations, such as '"{}: {1}".format(a,b)', will raise a ValueError.`
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5487652Z -           },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5487747Z -           help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5488105Z -             markdown: '# Formatting string mixes implicitly and explicitly numbered fields\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5489274Z -               'A formatting expression, that is an expression of the form `the_format.format(args)` or `format(the_format, args)`, can use explicitly numbered fields, like `{1}`, or implicitly numbered fields, such as `{}`, but it cannot use both. Doing so will raise a `ValueError`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5489456Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5491754Z +               'Unfortunately, this means that if more than one base class defines the same attribute, the leftmost base class will effectively override the attribute of the rightmost base class, even though the leftmost base class is not a subclass of the rightmost base class. Unless the methods in question are designed for inheritance, using `super`, then this implicit overriding may not be the desired behavior. Even if it is the desired behavior it makes the code hard to understand and maintain.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5491847Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5491941Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5492062Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5492371Z +               'There are a number of ways that might be used to address this issue:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5492783Z -               'Use either explicitly numbered fields or implicitly numbered fields, but be consistent.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5492864Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5493209Z +               '* Override the attribute in the subclass to implement the correct behavior.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5493653Z +               '* Modify the class hierarchy and move equivalent or redundant methods to a common super class.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5494147Z +               '* Modify the method hierarchy, breaking up complex methods into constituent parts.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5494356Z +               '* Use delegation rather than inheritance.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5494438Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5494624Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5496263Z +               'In this example the class `ThreadingTCPServer` inherits from `ThreadingMixIn` and from `TCPServer`. However, both these classes implement `process_request` which means that `ThreadingTCPServer` will inherit `process_request` from `ThreadingMixIn`. Consequently, the implementation of `process_request` in `TCPServer` will be ignored, which may not be the correct behavior.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5496809Z -               'In the following example the formatting uses both implicit, `{}`, and explicit, `{1}`, numbering for fields, which is illegal.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5496888Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5496971Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5497080Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5497234Z -               'def illegal_format():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5497413Z -               '    "{} {1}".format("spam", "eggs")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5497497Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5497653Z +               'class TCPServer(object):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5497762Z +               '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5498012Z +               '    def process_request(self, request, client_address):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5498223Z +               '        self.do_work(request, client_address)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5498411Z +               '        self.shutdown_request(request)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5498506Z -               '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5498594Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5498694Z +               '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5498838Z +               'class ThreadingMixIn:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5499107Z +               '    """Mix-in class to handle each request in a new thread."""\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5499246Z -               '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5499760Z -               '* Python Library Reference: [String Formatting.](https://docs.python.org/2/library/string.html#string-formatting)\n',
