2026-10-20T21:06:14.5503155Z +               '        t.start()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5503246Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5503528Z +               'class ThreadingTCPServer(ThreadingMixIn, TCPServer): pass\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5503668Z -               '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5504217Z -               'Use either explicitly numbered fields or implicitly numbered fields, but be consistent.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5504309Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5504405Z +               '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5505490Z +               'This can be fixed either by overriding the method, as shown in class `ThreadingTCPServerOverriding` or by ensuring that the functionality provided by the two base classes does not overlap, as shown in class `ThreadingTCPServerChangedHierarchy`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5505575Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5505703Z -               '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5506249Z -               'In the following example the formatting uses both implicit, `{}`, and explicit, `{1}`, numbering for fields, which is illegal.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5506420Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5506510Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5506625Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5506718Z +               '   \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5507143Z +               '#Fixed by overriding. This does not change behavior, but makes it explicit and comprehensible.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5507447Z +               'class ThreadingTCPServerOverriding(ThreadingMixIn, TCPServer):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5507541Z +               '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5507790Z +               '    def process_request(self, request, client_address):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5508237Z +               '        #process_request forwards to do_work, so it is OK to call ThreadingMixIn.process_request directly\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5508545Z +               '        ThreadingMixIn.process_request(self, request, client_address)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5508667Z +               '        \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5508823Z -               'def illegal_format():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5508999Z -               '    "{} {1}".format("spam", "eggs")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5509086Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5509395Z +               '#Fixed by separating threading functionality from request handling.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5509539Z +               'class ThreadingMixIn:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5509748Z +               '    """Mix-in class to help with threads."""\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5509843Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5510038Z +               '    def do_job_in_thread(self, job, args):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5510242Z +               '        """Start a new thread to do the job"""\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5510472Z +               '        t = threading.Thread(target = job, args = args)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5510614Z +               '        t.start()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5510709Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5511049Z +               'class ThreadingTCPServerChangedHierarchy(ThreadingMixIn, TCPServer):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5511269Z +               '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5511699Z +               '    def process_request(self, request, client_address):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5512131Z +               '        """Start a new thread to process the request."""\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5512445Z +               '        self.do_job_in_thread(self.do_work,  (request, client_address))\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5512546Z +               '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5512637Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5512729Z                 '```\n' +
