2026-10-20T21:06:14.5557424Z +             text: 'Class definition will raise a type error at runtime due to inconsistent method resolution order(MRO)'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5557957Z -             text: 'Including surplus keyword arguments in a formatting call makes code more difficult to read and may indicate an error.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5558041Z             },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5558122Z             help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5558353Z +             markdown: '# Inconsistent method resolution order\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5560590Z +               'Python 2.3 introduced new-style classes (classes inheriting from object). New-style classes use the C3 linearization method to determine a method resolution ordering (MRO) for each class. The C3 linearization method ensures that for a class C, if a class C1 precedes a class C2 in the MRO of C then C1 should also precede C2 in the MRO of all subclasses of C. It is possible to create a situation where it is impossible to achieve this consistency and this will guarantee that a ` TypeError` will be raised at runtime.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5560900Z -             markdown: '# Unused named argument in formatting call\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5562463Z -               'A formatting expression, that is an expression of the form `the_format.format(args)` or `format(the_format, args)` can have keyword arguments of any name, as long as all the required names are provided. However, surplus keyword arguments, those with names that are not in the format, are redundant. These surplus arguments clutter the code, making it harder to read.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5562552Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5562959Z -               'It is also possible that surplus keyword arguments indicate a mistake in the format string.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5563046Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5563142Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5563259Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5563473Z +               'Use a class hierarchy that is not ambiguous.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5563976Z -               'Check that the format string is correct and then remove any surplus keyword arguments.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5564063Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5564145Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5564262Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5565141Z +               'The MRO of class `X` is just `X, object`. The program will fail when the MRO of class `Y` needs to be calculated because `object` precedes `X` in the definition of `Y` but the opposite is true in the MRO of `X`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5565704Z -               'In the following example, the comment indicates that the `chips` keyword argument is no longer required and should be deleted.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5565792Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5565871Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5565980Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5566123Z +               'class X(object):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5566273Z +               '    def __init__(self):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5566495Z +               '        print("X")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5566634Z +               'class Y(object,X):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5566786Z +               '    def __init__(self):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5566922Z +               '        print("Y")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5567070Z -               'def surplus_argument():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5567361Z -               '    the_format = "{spam} {eggs}" # Used to be "{spam} {eggs} {chips}"\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5567679Z -               '    return the_format.format(spam = "spam", eggs="eggs", chips="chips")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5567769Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5567857Z                 '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5568058Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5568172Z                 '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5568629Z +               '* Python: [The Python 2.3 Method Resolution Order](http://www.python.org/download/releases/2.3/mro/).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5568837Z +             text: '# Inconsistent method resolution order\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5571042Z +               'Python 2.3 introduced new-style classes (classes inheriting from object). New-style classes use the C3 linearization method to determine a method resolution ordering (MRO) for each class. The C3 linearization method ensures that for a class C, if a class C1 precedes a class C2 in the MRO of C then C1 should also precede C2 in the MRO of all subclasses of C. It is possible to create a situation where it is impossible to achieve this consistency and this will guarantee that a ` TypeError` will be raised at runtime.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5571562Z -               '* Python Library Reference: [String Formatting.](https://docs.python.org/2/library/string.html#string-formatting)\n',
