2026-10-20T21:06:14.5585603Z             fullDescription: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5586118Z +             text: 'Using too many or too few arguments in a call to the `__init__` method of a class will result in a TypeError at runtime.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5586945Z -             text: `A string formatting operation, such as '"{name}".format(key=b)', where the names of format items in the format string differs from the names of the values to be formatted will raise a KeyError.`
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5587030Z             },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5587120Z             help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5587401Z +             markdown: '# Wrong number of arguments in a class instantiation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5587978Z +               'A call to the `__init__` method of a class must supply an argument for each parameter that does not have a default value defined, so:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5588314Z -             markdown: '# Missing named arguments in formatting call\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5589541Z -               'A formatting expression, that is an expression of the form `the_format.format(args)` or `format(the_format, args)`, can use named fields. If it does, then keyword arguments must be supplied for all named fields. If any of the keyword arguments are missing then a `KeyError` will be raised.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5589630Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5590008Z +               '* The minimum number of arguments is the number of parameters without default values.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5590862Z +               '* The maximum number of arguments is the total number of parameters, unless the class `__init__` method takes a varargs (starred) parameter in which case there is no limit.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5590954Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5591078Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5591565Z +               'If there are too few arguments then check to see which arguments have been omitted and supply values for those.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5591982Z -               'Change the format to match the arguments and ensure that the arguments have the correct names.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5592068Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5592499Z +               'If there are too many arguments then check to see if any have been added by mistake and remove those.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5592583Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5593194Z +               'Also check where a comma has been inserted instead of an operator or a dot. For example, the code is `obj,attr` when it should be `obj.attr`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5593284Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5594063Z +               'If it is not clear which are the missing or surplus arguments, then this suggests a logical error. The fix will then depend on the nature of the error.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5594241Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5594331Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5594447Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5595285Z -               'In the following example, if `unlikely_condition()` is true, then a `KeyError` will be raised as the keyword parameter `eggs` is missing. Adding a keyword parameter named `eggs` would fix this.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5595365Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5595460Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5595564Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5595716Z +               'class Point(object):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5595887Z +               '    def __init__(self, x, y):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5596023Z +               '        self.x = x\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5596159Z +               '        self.y = y\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5596322Z -               'def unsafe_named_format():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5596488Z -               '    the_format = "{spam} {eggs}"\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5596657Z -               '    if unlikely_condition():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5596987Z -               '        return the_format.format(spam="spam", completely_different="eggs")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5597107Z -               '    else:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5597364Z -               '        return the_format.format(spam="spam", eggs="eggs")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5597443Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5597666Z +               'p = Point(1)      # TypeError: too few arguments\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5597903Z +               'p = Point(1,2,3)  # TypeError: too many arguments\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5597993Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5598084Z                 '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5598167Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5598275Z                 '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5598682Z +               '* Python Glossary: [Arguments](https://docs.python.org/2/glossary.html#term-argument).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5599080Z +               '* Python Glossary: [Parameters](https://docs.python.org/glossary.html#term-parameter).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5599883Z +               '* Python Programming FAQ: [ What is the difference between arguments and parameters?](https://docs.python.org/2/faq/programming.html#faq-argument-vs-parameter).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5600461Z +               '* The Python Language Reference: [Data model: object.__init__](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/datamodel.html#object.__init__)\n' +
