2026-10-20T21:06:14.5646981Z -               'When you want to compare the value of two literals, use the comparison operator `==` or `!=` in place of `is` or `is not`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5647070Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5648136Z +               'The `functools.total_ordering` class decorator can be used to automatically implement all four comparison methods from a single one, which is typically the cleanest way to ensure all necessary comparison methods are implemented consistently.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5648613Z -               'If the uniqueness property or performance are important then use an object that does not redefine equality.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5648697Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5648780Z                 '\n' +
