2026-10-20T21:06:14.5700276Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5700393Z +               'class A:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5700552Z +               '    def __init__(self, a):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5700686Z +               '        self.a = a \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5700768Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5700951Z +               '    # BAD: ne is defined, but not eq.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5701109Z +               '    def __ne__(self, other):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5701290Z +               '        if not isinstance(other, A):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5701467Z +               '            return NotImplemented \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5701631Z +               '        return self.a != other.a\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5701772Z -               'class Customer:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5701943Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5702057Z +               'x = A(1)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5702176Z +               'y = A(1)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5702335Z -               '    def __init__(self, data):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5702486Z -               '        self.data = data\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5702573Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5702919Z +               'print(x == y) # Prints False (potentially unexpected - object identity is used)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5703079Z +               'print(x != y) # Prints False\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5703249Z -               '    def check_data(self, data):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5703567Z -               "        if data != data:  # Forgotten 'self'\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5703772Z -               '            raise Exception("Invalid data!")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5704058Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5704155Z +               '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.5704857Z +               'In the following example, `C` defines an `__eq__` method, but its `__ne__` implementation is inherited from `B`, which is not consistent with the equality operation.\n' +
