2026-10-20T21:06:14.6039198Z +             markdown: '# `__eq__` not overridden when adding attributes\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6039855Z +               'A class that defines attributes that are not present in its superclasses may need to override the `__eq__()` method (`__ne__()` should also be defined).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6040160Z -             markdown: '# Backspace escape in regular expression\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6041714Z -               'The meaning of the `\\b` escape sequence inside a regular expression depends on its syntactic context: inside a character class, it matches the backspace character; outside of a character class, it matches a word boundary. This context dependency makes regular expressions hard to read, so the `\\b` escape sequence should not be used inside character classes.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6041801Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6042416Z +               'Adding additional attributes without overriding `__eq__()` means that the additional attributes will not be accounted for in equality tests.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6042506Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6042599Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6042717Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6042879Z +               'Override the `__eq__` method.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6043284Z -               'Replace `\\b` in character classes with the semantically identical escape sequence `\\x08`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6043365Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6043447Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6043552Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6044313Z +               'In the following example the `ColorPoint` class subclasses the `Point` class and adds a new attribute, but does not override the `__eq__` method.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6045069Z -               'In the following example, the regular expression contains two uses of `\\b`: in the first case, it matches a word boundary, in the second case it matches a backspace character.\n' +
