2026-10-20T21:06:14.6120087Z             fullDescription: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6120511Z +             text: 'Using property descriptors in old-style classes does not work from Python 2.1 onward.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6121013Z -             text: 'Incomplete special groups are parsed as normal groups and are unlikely to match the intended strings.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6121095Z             },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6121184Z             help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6121395Z +             markdown: '# Property in old-style class\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6122204Z +               'Property descriptors are only supported for the new-style classes that were introduced in Python 2.1. Property descriptors should only be used in new-style classes.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6122513Z -             markdown: '# Missing part of special group in regular expression\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6124368Z -               'One of the problems with using regular expressions is that almost any sequence of characters is a valid pattern. This means that it is easy to omit a necessary character and still have a valid regular expression. Omitting a character in a named capturing group is a specific case which can dramatically change the meaning of a regular expression.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6124460Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6124550Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6124681Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6125634Z +               'If you want to define properties in a class, then ensure that the class is a new-style class. You can convert an old-style class to a new-style class by inheriting from `object`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6125946Z -               'Examine the regular expression to find and correct any typos.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6126036Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6126121Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6126240Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6127383Z +               'In the following example all the classes attempt to set a property for `x`. However, only the third and fourth classes are new-style classes. Consequently, the `x` property is only available for the `NewStyle` and `InheritNewStyle` classes.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6128929Z -               'In the following example, the regular expression for `matcher`, `r"(P<name>[\\w]+)"`, is missing a "?" and will match only strings of letters that start with "P&lt;name&gt;", instead of matching any sequence of letters and placing the result in a named group. The fixed version, `fixed_matcher`, includes the "?" and will work as expected.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6129018Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6129820Z +               'If you define the `OldStyle` class as inheriting from a new-style class, then the `x ` property would be available for both the `OldStyle` and `InheritOldStyle` classes.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6129972Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6130073Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6130190Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6130316Z -               'import re\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6130532Z -               "matcher = re.compile(r'(P<name>[\\w]+)')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6130615Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6130767Z +               'class OldStyle:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6130934Z -               'def only_letters(text):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6131101Z -               '    m = matcher.match(text)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6131230Z -               '    if m:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6131465Z -               `        print("Letters are: " + m.group('name'))\n` +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6131550Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6131717Z +               '    def __init__(self, x):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6131866Z +               '        self._x = x\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6131963Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6132363Z +               "    # Incorrect: 'OldStyle' is not a new-style class and '@property' is not supported\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6132500Z +               '    @property\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6132647Z +               '    def x(self):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6132804Z +               '        return self._x\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6132900Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6133000Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6133189Z +               'class InheritOldStyle(OldStyle):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6133283Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6133446Z +               '    def __init__(self, x):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6133594Z +               '        self._x = x\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6133692Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6134246Z +               "    # Incorrect: 'InheritOldStyle' is not a new-style class and '@property' is not supported\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6134384Z +               '    @property\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6134529Z +               '    def x(self):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6134764Z +               '        return self._x\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6134859Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6134957Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6135112Z +               'class NewStyle(object):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6135202Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6135358Z +               '    def __init__(self, x):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6135489Z +               '        self._x = x\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6135586Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6135924Z +               "    # Correct: 'NewStyle' is a new-style class and '@property' is supported\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6136051Z +               '    @property\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6136311Z +               '    def x(self):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6136464Z +               '        return self._x\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6136554Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6136741Z +               'class InheritNewStyle(NewStyle):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6136836Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6136987Z +               '    def __init__(self, x):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6137126Z +               '        self._x = x\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6137216Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6137643Z +               "    # Correct: 'InheritNewStyle' inherits from a new-style class and '@property' is supported\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6137776Z +               '    @property\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6137905Z +               '    def x(self):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6138052Z +               '        return self._x\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6138148Z +               '\n' +
