2026-10-20T21:06:14.6142504Z +               'Property descriptors are only supported for the new-style classes that were introduced in Python 2.1. Property descriptors should only be used in new-style classes.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6142986Z -               '* Python Standard Library: [Regular expression operations](https://docs.python.org/library/re.html).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6143464Z -               '* Regular-Expressions.info: [Named Capturing Groups](http://www.regular-expressions.info/named.html).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6143753Z -             text: '# Missing part of special group in regular expression\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6145519Z -               'One of the problems with using regular expressions is that almost any sequence of characters is a valid pattern. This means that it is easy to omit a necessary character and still have a valid regular expression. Omitting a character in a named capturing group is a specific case which can dramatically change the meaning of a regular expression.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6145609Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6145698Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6145829Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6146620Z +               'If you want to define properties in a class, then ensure that the class is a new-style class. You can convert an old-style class to a new-style class by inheriting from `object`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6147004Z -               'Examine the regular expression to find and correct any typos.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6147092Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6147171Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6147286Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6148485Z +               'In the following example all the classes attempt to set a property for `x`. However, only the third and fourth classes are new-style classes. Consequently, the `x` property is only available for the `NewStyle` and `InheritNewStyle` classes.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6149956Z -               'In the following example, the regular expression for `matcher`, `r"(P<name>[\\w]+)"`, is missing a "?" and will match only strings of letters that start with "P&lt;name&gt;", instead of matching any sequence of letters and placing the result in a named group. The fixed version, `fixed_matcher`, includes the "?" and will work as expected.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6150049Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6150811Z +               'If you define the `OldStyle` class as inheriting from a new-style class, then the `x ` property would be available for both the `OldStyle` and `InheritOldStyle` classes.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6150894Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6150992Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6151107Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6151229Z -               'import re\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6151438Z -               "matcher = re.compile(r'(P<name>[\\w]+)')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6151521Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6151664Z +               'class OldStyle:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6151822Z -               'def only_letters(text):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6152056Z -               '    m = matcher.match(text)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6152182Z -               '    if m:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6152408Z -               `        print("Letters are: " + m.group('name'))\n` +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6152488Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6152651Z +               '    def __init__(self, x):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6152791Z +               '        self._x = x\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6152880Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6153263Z +               "    # Incorrect: 'OldStyle' is not a new-style class and '@property' is not supported\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6153393Z +               '    @property\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6153532Z +               '    def x(self):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6153682Z +               '        return self._x\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6153915Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6154019Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6154205Z +               'class InheritOldStyle(OldStyle):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6154299Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6154458Z +               '    def __init__(self, x):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6154601Z +               '        self._x = x\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6154690Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6155108Z +               "    # Incorrect: 'InheritOldStyle' is not a new-style class and '@property' is not supported\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6155236Z +               '    @property\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6155375Z +               '    def x(self):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6155525Z +               '        return self._x\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6155617Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6155712Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6155868Z +               'class NewStyle(object):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6155958Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6156180Z +               '    def __init__(self, x):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6156433Z +               '        self._x = x\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6156591Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6157106Z +               "    # Correct: 'NewStyle' is a new-style class and '@property' is supported\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6157402Z +               '    @property\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6157543Z +               '    def x(self):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6157691Z +               '        return self._x\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6157781Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6157964Z +               'class InheritNewStyle(NewStyle):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6158060Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6158213Z +               '    def __init__(self, x):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6158353Z +               '        self._x = x\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6158446Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6159022Z +               "    # Correct: 'InheritNewStyle' inherits from a new-style class and '@property' is supported\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6159161Z +               '    @property\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6159294Z +               '    def x(self):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6159448Z +               '        return self._x\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6159546Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6159757Z -               "#Fix the pattern by adding the missing '?'\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6159988Z -               "fixed_matcher = re.compile(r'(?P<name>[\\w]+)')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6160079Z                 '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6160160Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6160278Z                 '## References\n' +
