2026-10-20T21:06:14.6170079Z             },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6170196Z             fullDescription: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6170763Z +             text: 'Descriptor objects can be shared across many instances. Mutating them can cause strange side effects or race conditions.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6171221Z -             text: 'Duplicate characters in a class have no effect and may indicate an error in the regular expression.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6171309Z             },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6171396Z             help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6171694Z +             markdown: '# Mutation of descriptor in `__get__` or `__set__` method\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6172462Z +               'The descriptor protocol allows user programmable attribute access. The descriptor protocol is what enables class methods, static methods, properties and `super()`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6172754Z -             markdown: '# Duplication in regular expression character class\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6174008Z -               'Character classes in regular expressions represent sets of characters, so there is no need to specify the same character twice in one character class. Duplicate characters in character classes are at best useless, and may even indicate a latent bug.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6174182Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6175225Z +               'Descriptor objects are class attributes which control the behavior of instance attributes. Consequently, a single descriptor is common to all instances of a class and should not be mutated when instance attributes are accessed.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6175305Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6175402Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6175531Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6175981Z +               'Do not mutate the descriptor object, rather create a new object that contains the necessary state.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6177128Z -               'Determine whether a character is simply duplicated or whether the character class was in fact meant as a group. If it is just a duplicate, then remove the duplicate character. If was supposed to be a group, then replace the square brackets with parentheses.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6177227Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6177307Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6177421Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6177906Z +               'In this example the descriptor class `MutatingDescriptor` stores a reference to `obj` in an attribute.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6179302Z -               'In the following example, the character class `[password|pwd]` contains two instances each of the characters `d`, `p`, `s`, and `w`. The programmer most likely meant to write `(password|pwd)` (a pattern that matches either the string `"password"` or the string `"pwd"`), and accidentally mistyped the enclosing brackets.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6179392Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6179478Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6179585Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6179719Z -               'import re\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6179930Z -               'matcher = re.compile(r"[password|pwd]")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6180093Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6180373Z +               '#This is prone to strange side effects and race conditions.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6180559Z +               'class MutatingDescriptor(object):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6180667Z +               '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6180838Z +               '    def __init__(self, func):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6180995Z +               '        self.my_func = func\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6181119Z +               '        \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6181308Z +               '    def __get__(self, obj, obj_type):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6181779Z +               '        #Modified state is visible to all instances of C that might call "show".\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6181943Z +               '        self.my_obj = obj\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6182092Z +               '        return self\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6182210Z +               '        \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6182381Z +               '    def __call__(self, *args):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6182595Z +               '        return self.my_func(self.my_obj, *args)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6182698Z +               '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6182839Z +               'def show(obj):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6182971Z +               '    print (obj)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6183075Z +               '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6183220Z +               'class C(object):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6183315Z +               '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6183487Z +               '    def __init__(self, value):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6183641Z +               '        self.value = value\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6183767Z +               '        \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6184058Z +               '    def __str__(self):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6184251Z +               '        return ("C: " + str(self.value))\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6184445Z +               '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6184639Z +               '    show = MutatingDescriptor(show)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6184738Z +               '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6184868Z +               'c1 = C(1)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6184995Z +               'c1.show()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6185113Z +               'c2 = C(2)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6185236Z +               'c2.show()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6185368Z +               'c1_show = c1.show\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6185476Z +               'c2.show\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6185599Z +               'c1_show()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6185756Z -               'def find_password(data):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6185920Z -               '    if matcher.match(data):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6186100Z -               '        print("Found password!")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6186180Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6186304Z +               '#Outputs:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6186400Z +               '#C: 1\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6186504Z +               '#C: 2\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6186603Z +               '#C: 2\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6186688Z                 '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6187255Z +               'In the following example, the descriptor class `NonMutatingDescriptor` returns a new object every time `__get__` is called.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6187653Z -               'To fix this problem, the regular expression should be rewritten to `r"(password|pwd)"`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6187734Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6187818Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6187942Z +               '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6188072Z +               'import types\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6188167Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6188374Z +               '#Immutable version, which is safe to share.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6188572Z +               'class NonMutatingDescriptor(object):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6188675Z +               '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6188838Z +               '    def __init__(self, func):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6188997Z +               '        self.my_func = func\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6189194Z +               '        \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6189377Z +               '    def __get__(self, obj, obj_type):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6189582Z +               '        #Return a new object to each access.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6189811Z +               '        return types.MethodType(self.my_func, obj)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6189908Z +               '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6190046Z +               'def show(obj):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6190176Z +               '    print (obj)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6190279Z +               '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6190422Z +               'class C(object):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6190637Z +               '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6190813Z +               '    def __init__(self, value):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6190969Z +               '        self.value = value\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6191088Z +               '        \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6191238Z +               '    def __str__(self):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6191432Z +               '        return ("C: " + str(self.value))\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6191526Z +               '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6191723Z +               '    show = NonMutatingDescriptor(show)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6191818Z +               '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6191942Z +               'c1 = C(1)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6192068Z +               'c1.show()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6192183Z +               'c2 = C(2)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6192309Z +               'c2.show()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6192444Z +               'c1_show = c1.show\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6192546Z +               'c2.show\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6192673Z +               'c1_show()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6192763Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6192888Z +               '#Outputs:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6192992Z +               '#C: 1\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6193144Z +               '#C: 2\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6193252Z +               '#C: 1\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6193355Z +               '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6193446Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6193567Z                 '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6194244Z +               '* Python Language Reference: [Implementing Descriptors.](https://docs.python.org/reference/datamodel.html#descriptors)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6194697Z +               "* Mark Lutz. *Learning Python*, Section 30.6: Methods Are Objects: Bound or Unbound. O'Reilly 2013.\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6195095Z +               '* A real world example: [NumPy Issue 5247.](https://github.com/numpy/numpy/issues/5247)\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6195382Z +             text: '# Mutation of descriptor in `__get__` or `__set__` method\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6196155Z +               'The descriptor protocol allows user programmable attribute access. The descriptor protocol is what enables class methods, static methods, properties and `super()`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6196643Z -               '* Python Standard Library: [Regular expression operations](https://docs.python.org/library/re.html).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6197221Z -               '* Regular-Expressions.info: [Character Classes or Character Sets](http://www.regular-expressions.info/charclass.html).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6197489Z -             text: '# Duplication in regular expression character class\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6198627Z -               'Character classes in regular expressions represent sets of characters, so there is no need to specify the same character twice in one character class. Duplicate characters in character classes are at best useless, and may even indicate a latent bug.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6198718Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6199753Z +               'Descriptor objects are class attributes which control the behavior of instance attributes. Consequently, a single descriptor is common to all instances of a class and should not be mutated when instance attributes are accessed.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6199848Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6200056Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6200181Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6200637Z +               'Do not mutate the descriptor object, rather create a new object that contains the necessary state.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6201790Z -               'Determine whether a character is simply duplicated or whether the character class was in fact meant as a group. If it is just a duplicate, then remove the duplicate character. If was supposed to be a group, then replace the square brackets with parentheses.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6201872Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6201958Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6202193Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6202673Z +               'In this example the descriptor class `MutatingDescriptor` stores a reference to `obj` in an attribute.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6204198Z -               'In the following example, the character class `[password|pwd]` contains two instances each of the characters `d`, `p`, `s`, and `w`. The programmer most likely meant to write `(password|pwd)` (a pattern that matches either the string `"password"` or the string `"pwd"`), and accidentally mistyped the enclosing brackets.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6204296Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6204377Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6204491Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6204610Z -               'import re\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6204826Z -               'matcher = re.compile(r"[password|pwd]")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6204910Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6205184Z +               '#This is prone to strange side effects and race conditions.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6205377Z +               'class MutatingDescriptor(object):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6205481Z +               '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6205726Z +               '    def __init__(self, func):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6205891Z +               '        self.my_func = func\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6206017Z +               '        \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6206202Z +               '    def __get__(self, obj, obj_type):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6206557Z +               '        #Modified state is visible to all instances of C that might call "show".\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6206714Z +               '        self.my_obj = obj\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6206856Z +               '        return self\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6206975Z +               '        \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6207140Z +               '    def __call__(self, *args):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6207357Z +               '        return self.my_func(self.my_obj, *args)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6207464Z +               '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6207598Z +               'def show(obj):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6207743Z +               '    print (obj)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6207847Z +               '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6207983Z +               'class C(object):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6208093Z +               '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6208260Z +               '    def __init__(self, value):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6208419Z +               '        self.value = value\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6208545Z +               '        \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6208691Z +               '    def __str__(self):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6208885Z +               '        return ("C: " + str(self.value))\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6208985Z +               '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6209167Z +               '    show = MutatingDescriptor(show)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6209271Z +               '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6209399Z +               'c1 = C(1)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6209520Z +               'c1.show()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6209651Z +               'c2 = C(2)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6209771Z +               'c2.show()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6209912Z +               'c1_show = c1.show\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6210018Z +               'c2.show\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6210137Z +               'c1_show()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6210387Z -               'def find_password(data):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6210558Z -               '    if matcher.match(data):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6210731Z -               '        print("Found password!")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6210818Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6210941Z +               '#Outputs:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6211047Z +               '#C: 1\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6211151Z +               '#C: 2\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6211247Z +               '#C: 2\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6211340Z                 '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6212050Z +               'In the following example, the descriptor class `NonMutatingDescriptor` returns a new object every time `__get__` is called.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6212462Z -               'To fix this problem, the regular expression should be rewritten to `r"(password|pwd)"`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6212555Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6212641Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6212767Z +               '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6212901Z +               'import types\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6212991Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6213208Z +               '#Immutable version, which is safe to share.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6213409Z +               'class NonMutatingDescriptor(object):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6213504Z +               '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6213676Z +               '    def __init__(self, func):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6213976Z +               '        self.my_func = func\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6214096Z +               '        \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6214290Z +               '    def __get__(self, obj, obj_type):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6214495Z +               '        #Return a new object to each access.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6214722Z +               '        return types.MethodType(self.my_func, obj)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6214914Z +               '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6215047Z +               'def show(obj):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6215188Z +               '    print (obj)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6215290Z +               '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6215427Z +               'class C(object):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6215527Z +               '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6215693Z +               '    def __init__(self, value):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6215847Z +               '        self.value = value\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6215967Z +               '        \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6216116Z +               '    def __str__(self):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6216304Z +               '        return ("C: " + str(self.value))\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6216404Z +               '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6216600Z +               '    show = NonMutatingDescriptor(show)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6216703Z +               '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6216826Z +               'c1 = C(1)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6216945Z +               'c1.show()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6217072Z +               'c2 = C(2)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6217196Z +               'c2.show()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6217331Z +               'c1_show = c1.show\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6217438Z +               'c2.show\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6217559Z +               'c1_show()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6217656Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6217781Z +               '#Outputs:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6217877Z +               '#C: 1\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6217979Z +               '#C: 2\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6218081Z +               '#C: 1\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6218174Z +               '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6218269Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6218386Z                 '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6218963Z +               '* Python Language Reference: [Implementing Descriptors.](https://docs.python.org/reference/datamodel.html#descriptors)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6219416Z +               "* Mark Lutz. *Learning Python*, Section 30.6: Methods Are Objects: Bound or Unbound. O'Reilly 2013.\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6219890Z +               '* A real world example: [NumPy Issue 5247.](https://github.com/numpy/numpy/issues/5247)\n'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6220377Z -               '* Python Standard Library: [Regular expression operations](https://docs.python.org/library/re.html).\n' +
