2026-10-20T21:06:14.6361590Z -             level: 'error'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6361672Z             },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6361783Z             fullDescription: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6362356Z +             text: "Importing a module using 'import *' may unintentionally pollute the global namespace if the module does not define `__all__`"
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6362888Z -             text: 'Method has a different signature from the overridden method and, if it were called, would be likely to cause an error.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6363042Z             },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6363129Z             help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6363342Z +             markdown: "# 'import *' may pollute namespace\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6365609Z +               'When you import a module using `from xxx import *` all public names defined in the module are imported and bound in the local namespace of the `import` statement. The public names are determined by checking the `__all__` variable for the module. If ` __all__` is not defined then all names within the module that do not start with an underscore character are imported. This pollutes the current namespace with names that are not part of the public API for the module.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6365950Z -             markdown: '# Mismatch between signature and use of an overriding method\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6367120Z -               'There is a call to the overridden method, and potentially the overriding method, with arguments that are not legal for the overriding method. This will cause an error if the overriding method is called and is a violation of the Liskov substitution principle.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6367209Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6367297Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6367424Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6367634Z +               'There are two ways to address this problem:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6368113Z -               'Ensure that the overriding method accepts all the parameters that are legal for the overridden method.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6368205Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6368768Z +               '* where possible, modify the module being imported *from* and define `__all__ ` to restrict the names to be imported\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6369118Z +               '* otherwise, explicitly import the values that you need.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6369209Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6369320Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6369779Z +               'The following simple example shows how `__all__` controls the public names for the module `finance`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6371730Z -               'In this example there is a mismatch between the legal parameters for the base class method `(self, source, filename, symbol)` and the extension method `(self, source)`. The extension method can be used to override the base method as long as values are not specified for the `filename` and (optional) `symbol` parameters. If the extension method was passed the additional parameters accepted by the base method then an error would occur.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6371812Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6371896Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6372008Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6372185Z +               '# Example module - finance.py\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6372271Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6372584Z +               "__all__ = ['tax1', 'tax2']  #defines the names to import when '*' is used\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6372753Z -               'class BaseClass(object):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6372838Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6372956Z +               'tax1 = 5\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6373082Z +               'tax2 = 10\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6373246Z +               "def cost(): return 'cost'\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6373488Z -               '    def run(self, source, filename, symbol="single"):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6373646Z -               '        ... # Definition\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6373733Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6374018Z +               '# Imported into code using\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6374218Z -               '    def load_and_run(self, filename):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6374401Z -               '        source = self.load(filename)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6374848Z -               '        self.run(source, filename) # Matches signature in this class, but not in the derived class.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6375023Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6375172Z +               'from finance import *\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6375358Z -               'class DerivedClass(BaseClass):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6375444Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6375572Z +               'print tax1\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6375702Z +               'print tax2\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6375864Z -               '    def run(self, source):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6376009Z -               '        ... # Definition\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6376105Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6376307Z                 '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6376991Z +               'If the `finance` module did not include a definition of `__all__`, then you could replace `from finance import *` with `from finance import tax1, tax2`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6377567Z -               'The extension method should be updated to support the `filename` and `symbol` parameters supported by the overridden method.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6377653Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6377744Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6377864Z                 '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6378399Z +               '* Python Language Reference: [The import statement](http://docs.python.org/2/reference/simple_stmts.html#import).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6378761Z +               '* Python Tutorial: [Modules](http://docs.python.org/2/tutorial/modules.html).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6378966Z +             text: "# 'import *' may pollute namespace\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6381033Z +               'When you import a module using `from xxx import *` all public names defined in the module are imported and bound in the local namespace of the `import` statement. The public names are determined by checking the `__all__` variable for the module. If ` __all__` is not defined then all names within the module that do not start with an underscore character are imported. This pollutes the current namespace with names that are not part of the public API for the module.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6381969Z -               '* Wikipedia: [Liskov Substitution Principle](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liskov_substitution_principle), [Method overriding](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Method_overriding#Python).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6382277Z -             text: '# Mismatch between signature and use of an overriding method\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6383448Z -               'There is a call to the overridden method, and potentially the overriding method, with arguments that are not legal for the overriding method. This will cause an error if the overriding method is called and is a violation of the Liskov substitution principle.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6383532Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6383618Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6383749Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6384080Z +               'There are two ways to address this problem:\n' +
