2026-10-20T21:06:14.6403295Z             help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6403497Z +             markdown: '# Import of deprecated module\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6404620Z +               'A module is deprecated when it cannot or will not be maintained indefinitely in the standard library. Deprecated modules may not receive security fixes or other important updates. See PEP 4 for a list of all deprecated modules.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6404910Z -             markdown: '# Iterator does not return self from `__iter__` method\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6406092Z -               'Iterator classes (classes defining a `__next__` method) should have an `__iter__` method that returns the iterator itself. This ensures that the object is also an iterable; and behaves as expected when used anywhere an iterator or iterable is expected, such as in `for` loops.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6406183Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6406262Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6406387Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6406823Z +               'Do not import the deprecated module. Replace uses of it with uses of a better maintained module.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6407254Z -               'Ensure that the `__iter__` method returns `self`, or is otherwise equivalent as an iterator to `self`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6407345Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6407430Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6407553Z -               '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6408298Z -               "In the following example, the `MyRange` class's `__iter__` method does not return `self`. This would lead to unexpected results when used with a `for` loop or `in` statement.\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6408482Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6408572Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6408699Z -               '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6408852Z -               'class MyRange(object):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6409031Z -               '    def __init__(self, low, high):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6409191Z -               '        self.current = low\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6409338Z -               '        self.high = high\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6409439Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6409592Z -               '    def __iter__(self):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6410083Z -               '        return (self.current, self.high) # BAD: does not return `self`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6410187Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6410331Z -               '    def __next__(self):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6410520Z -               '        if self.current > self.high:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6410664Z -               '            return None\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6410818Z -               '        self.current += 1\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6410993Z -               '        return self.current - 1\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6411098Z -               '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6411189Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6411313Z                 '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6411778Z +               '* Python PEPs: [PEP 4 -- Deprecation of Standard Modules ](http://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0004/).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6412182Z +               '* Common Weakness Enumeration: [CWE-477](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/477.html).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6412372Z +             text: '# Import of deprecated module\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6413375Z +               'A module is deprecated when it cannot or will not be maintained indefinitely in the standard library. Deprecated modules may not receive security fixes or other important updates. See PEP 4 for a list of all deprecated modules.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6414081Z -               '* Python Language Reference: [object.__iter__](http://docs.python.org/3/reference/datamodel.html#object.__iter__).\n' +
