2026-10-20T21:06:14.6428624Z             fullDescription: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6429150Z +             text: 'Importing the value of a mutable attribute directly means that changes in global state will not be observed locally.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6429958Z -             text: 'Method has a signature that differs from both the signature of its overriding methods and the arguments with which it is called, and if it were called, would be likely to cause an error.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6430042Z             },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6430121Z             help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6430347Z +             markdown: '# Importing value of mutable attribute\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6431247Z +               'Explicitly importing an attribute from a module into the current namespace means that the value of that attribute will not be updated if the value in the original module changes.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6431567Z -             markdown: '# Mismatch between signature and use of an overridden method\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6432688Z -               'There is a call to the overriding method, and potentially the overridden method, with arguments that are not legal for the overridden method. This will cause an error if the overridden method is called and is a violation of the Liskov substitution principle.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6432781Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6433320Z +               'This can mean that changes in global state are not observed locally, which may lead to inconsistencies and possible errors.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6433410Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6433507Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6433628Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6434597Z +               'Instead of using `from module import attr`, simply import the module using `import module` and replace all uses of `attr` with `module.attr`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6435165Z -               'Ensure that the overridden method accepts all the parameters that are legal for overriding method(s).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6435251Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6435336Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6435443Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6436357Z +               'In the first of the two modules shown below, `from sys import stdout` is used to import the `stdout` attribute, rather than using `import sys` to import the module. Then `stdout` is used in the `main()` function.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6437878Z -               'In this example there is a mismatch between the legal parameters for the base class method `(self, source, filename)` and the extension method `(self, source)`. Since there is a call that uses the signature of the extension method then it can be inferred that the base signature is erroneous and should be updated to match that of the extension method.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6437964Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6438045Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6438154Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6438303Z +               'from sys import stdout\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6438393Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6438527Z +               'def main():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6438701Z +               '    stdout.write("Hello World!")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6438803Z +               '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6438962Z -               'class BaseClass(object):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6439041Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6439141Z +               '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6440751Z +               'In the second module, below, a function, `redirect_to_file` is defined to collect the output from `sys.stdout` and save it to a file. However, `redirect_to_file` will not work correctly when passed the `main()` function. This is because the `main()` function will not see the change to `sys.stdout`, as it uses its own version of `stdout` that was defined when the module was loaded.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6440992Z -               '    def run(self, source, filename, symbol="single"):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6441221Z -               '        ... # Definition\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6441307Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6441492Z -               '    def load_and_run(self, filename):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6441676Z -               '        source = self.load(filename)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6442043Z -               '        self.run(source) # Matches signature in derived class, but not in this class.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6442124Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6442248Z +               '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6442371Z +               'import sys\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6442549Z -               'class DerivedClass(BaseClass):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6442752Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6443010Z +               'def redirect_to_file(function, args, kwargs, filename):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6443191Z +               '    with open(filename) as out:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6443361Z +               '        orig_stdout = sys.stdout\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6443508Z +               '        sys.stdout = out\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6443639Z +               '        try:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6443945Z +               '            function(*args, **kwargs)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6444083Z +               '        finally:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6444264Z +               '            sys.stdout = orig_stdout\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6444420Z -               '    def run(self, source):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6444569Z -               '        ... # Definition\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6444653Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6444740Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6444827Z                 '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6445374Z +               'The problem can be fixed by rewriting the first module to import the `sys` module and write to `sys.stdout`, as shown below.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6445944Z -               'The base method should be updated to either remove the `filename` parameters, or add a default value for it.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6446034Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6446117Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6446235Z +               '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6446362Z +               'import sys\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6446452Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6446581Z +               'def main():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6446763Z +               '    sys.stdout.write("Hello World!")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6446855Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6446953Z +               '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6447048Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6447157Z                 '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6447686Z +               '* Python Language Reference: [The import statement](http://docs.python.org/2/reference/simple_stmts.html#import).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6448036Z +               '* Python Tutorial: [Modules](http://docs.python.org/2/tutorial/modules.html).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6448244Z +             text: '# Importing value of mutable attribute\n' +
