2026-10-20T21:06:14.6502917Z +             text: 'Syntax errors cause failures at runtime and prevent analysis of the code.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6503101Z -             text: '`__init__` method is a generator.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6503184Z             },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6503264Z             help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6503423Z +             markdown: '# Syntax error\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6504246Z +               'Syntax errors prevent a module being evaluated and thus imported. An attempt to import a module with invalid syntax will fail; a `SyntaxError` will be raised.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6504461Z -             markdown: '# `__init__` method is a generator\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6505658Z -               'The `__init__` method of a class is used to initialize new objects, not create them. As such, it should not return any value. By including a `yield` expression in the method turns it into a generator method. On calling it will return a generator resulting in a runtime error.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6505806Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6507028Z +               'A common cause of syntax errors is the difference in syntax between Python 2 and Python 3. In particular, a syntax error may be alerted if a Python 3 file is assumed to be compatible with Python 2 (or vice versa). Explicitly specifying the expected Python version can help prevent this.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6507117Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6508119Z +               'The existence of a syntax error in a module may suggest other problems as well. Either the module is never imported in practice and could be deleted or a `try` statement around the import is mistakenly discarding the `SyntaxError`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6508211Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6508305Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6508427Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6509165Z +               'Fixing the syntax error is the obvious fix. However, it is worth investigating why a module containing a syntax error was able to persist and address that problem as well.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6509832Z -               'The presence of a `yield` expression in an `__init__` method suggests a logical error, so it is not possible to suggest a general fix.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6509920Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6512215Z +               'If you suspect that the syntax error is caused by the analysis using the wrong version of Python, consider specifying the version explicitly. When you run code scanning using the CodeQL action, you can configure the Python version to use. For more information, see [Analyzing Python dependencies](https://docs.github.com/en/code-security/code-scanning/automatically-scanning-your-code-for-vulnerabilities-and-errors/configuring-code-scanning#analyzing-python-dependencies).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6512308Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6512440Z -               '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6512959Z -               'In this example the `__init__` method contains a yield expression. This is not logical in the context of an initializer.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6513050Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6513184Z +               '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6513604Z +               '* Python Tutorial: [SyntaxErrors.](http://docs.python.org/tutorial/errors.html#syntax-errors)\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6513758Z +             text: '# Syntax error\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6514574Z +               'Syntax errors prevent a module being evaluated and thus imported. An attempt to import a module with invalid syntax will fail; a `SyntaxError` will be raised.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6514658Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6515883Z +               'A common cause of syntax errors is the difference in syntax between Python 2 and Python 3. In particular, a syntax error may be alerted if a Python 3 file is assumed to be compatible with Python 2 (or vice versa). Explicitly specifying the expected Python version can help prevent this.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6516089Z -               '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6516268Z -               'class InitIsGenerator(object):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6516430Z -               '    def __init__(self, i):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6516564Z -               '        yield i\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6516659Z -               '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6516743Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6517738Z +               'The existence of a syntax error in a module may suggest other problems as well. Either the module is never imported in practice and could be deleted or a `try` statement around the import is mistakenly discarding the `SyntaxError`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6517832Z +               '\n' +
