2026-10-20T21:06:14.6547256Z +             text: 'Importing a module a second time has no effect and impairs readability'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6547667Z -             text: 'By the PEP8 style guide, the first parameter of a normal method should be named `self`.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6547753Z             },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6547836Z             help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6548061Z +             markdown: '# Module is imported more than once\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6548629Z +               'Importing the same module more than once has no effect as each module is only loaded once. It also confuses readers of the code.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6548911Z -             markdown: "# First parameter of a method is not named 'self'\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6549369Z -               'Normal methods should have at least one parameter and the first parameter should be called `self`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6549451Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6549536Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6549738Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6549898Z +               'Remove the second import.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6550426Z -               'Ensure that the first parameter of a normal method is named `self`, as recommended by the style guidelines in PEP 8.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6550513Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6551117Z -               'If a `self` parameter is unneeded, the method should be decorated with `staticmethod`, or moved out of the class as a regular function.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6551204Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6551299Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6551406Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6552056Z -               'In the following cases, the first argument of `Point.__init__` is named `val` instead; whereas in `Point2.__init__` it is correctly named `self`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6552144Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6552239Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6552355Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6552489Z +               'import module1\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6552634Z +               'import module2\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6552825Z +               'import module1 # Duplicate import\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6552958Z -               'class Point:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6553268Z -               "    def __init__(val, x, y):  # BAD: first parameter is mis-named 'val'\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6553412Z -               '        val._x = x\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6553543Z -               '        val._y = y\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6553629Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6553766Z -               'class Point2:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6554224Z -               "    def __init__(self, x, y):  # GOOD: first parameter is correctly named 'self'\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6554370Z -               '        self._x = x\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6554505Z -               '        self._y = y\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6554593Z                 '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6554680Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6554791Z                 '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6555214Z +               '* Python: [import statement](http://docs.python.org/reference/simple_stmts.html#import).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6555514Z +             text: '# Module is imported more than once\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6556085Z +               'Importing the same module more than once has no effect as each module is only loaded once. It also confuses readers of the code.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6556653Z -               '* Python PEP 8: [Function and method arguments](http://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0008/#function-and-method-arguments).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6557018Z -               '* Python Tutorial: [Classes](http://docs.python.org/2/tutorial/classes.html).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6557567Z -               '* Python Docs: [staticmethod](https://docs.python.org/3/library/functions.html#staticmethod).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6557831Z -             text: "# First parameter of a method is not named 'self'\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6558291Z -               'Normal methods should have at least one parameter and the first parameter should be called `self`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6558377Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6558465Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6558590Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6558746Z +               'Remove the second import.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6559270Z -               'Ensure that the first parameter of a normal method is named `self`, as recommended by the style guidelines in PEP 8.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6559356Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6559963Z -               'If a `self` parameter is unneeded, the method should be decorated with `staticmethod`, or moved out of the class as a regular function.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6560049Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6560140Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6560252Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6560964Z -               'In the following cases, the first argument of `Point.__init__` is named `val` instead; whereas in `Point2.__init__` it is correctly named `self`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6561048Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6561144Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6561255Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6561386Z +               'import module1\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6561522Z +               'import module2\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6561708Z +               'import module1 # Duplicate import\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6561839Z -               'class Point:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6562145Z -               "    def __init__(val, x, y):  # BAD: first parameter is mis-named 'val'\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6562282Z -               '        val._x = x\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6562427Z -               '        val._y = y\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6562513Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6562644Z -               'class Point2:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6562985Z -               "    def __init__(self, x, y):  # GOOD: first parameter is correctly named 'self'\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6563131Z -               '        self._x = x\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6563267Z -               '        self._y = y\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6563358Z                 '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6563446Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6563556Z                 '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6564090Z +               '* Python: [import statement](http://docs.python.org/reference/simple_stmts.html#import).\n'
